laurel mu 0102 (DarwinBoot, external/UniXNU/drivers/DarwinBoot): window fallback and platform limits.
(1) When no UEFI run holds the window the ADT asks for (darwinboot-memory-size), DarwinBoot takes the biggest window a usable run
holds (2 MiB multiple, >= 256 MiB) and passes that size to XNU (boot_args memSize = memSizeActual), instead of stopping with
"NO WINDOW". Screen line "WINDOW <size> OF <asked> @ <base>" and a DEBUG line. No usable run: "NO WINDOW" + the FREE list, as before.
(2) Two C defines a platform DSC may set (laurel mu 0103 does; without them DarwinBoot behaves as before, e.g. for negroni):
DARWINBOOT_MAX_WINDOW caps the window (Mi A3 TOPAZ_4K kernel: start.s bootstrap tables map the whole window; 4608 MiB fits the
16-page budget), DARWINBOOT_LOW4G_MIN makes a run usable only when the window starts below 4 GiB with at least that much below 4 GiB
(Mi A3: 256 MiB; USB/UFS DMA and the MDP scanout need kernel RAM below 4 GiB). XNU patch 2100 then reports
"LAUREL RAM: on: ... ; DarwinBoot gave N of the M MiB the ADT asks". scripts/laurel/mu-build.sh applies it to the DarwinBoot submodule
of UniXNU (paths start with DarwinBootPkg/).
